.TH env_put 3
.SH NAME
env_put, env_putb, env_put2, env_put2b \- modify the current environment
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <env.h>

.B int env_put(const char* \fIs\fP);
.br
.B int env_putb(const char* \fIx\fP, size_t \fIn\fP);
.br
.B int env_put2(const char* \fIs\fP, const char* \fIt\fP);
.br
.B int env_put2b(const char* \fIs\fP, const char* \fIt\fP, size_t \fIn\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions add or update variables in the process environment (\fIenviron\fP).
.B env_put
takes a "KEY=VALUE" string.
.B env_putb
takes a "KEY=VALUE" string of length \fIn\fP.
.B env_put2
and
.B env_put2b
take separate arguments for the key and the value.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 on failure (memory allocation).